hey remain unchanged.\n\nI should also check if there are any other patterns, like the placement of 5s or 2s, but in the test input, I don't see any 5s or 2s, so maybe those aren't relevant here. The key seems to be the transformation of 3s into 3s and 6s into 6s in specific positions.\n\nPutting it all together, the output for the test input should have 3s in the middle regions and 6s in the lower parts, with zeros elsewhere. This matches the structure seen in the training examples, so I'm confident this is the correct approach.\n",
